/2036532795984715896\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://xcancel.com/soraofficialapp/status/20365327959847158...\u003c/a\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/digital/openai-shutting-down-sora-ai-video-app-1236546187/\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/digital/openai-sh...\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://archive.ph/ABkeI\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://archive.ph/ABkeI\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47508246\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47508246\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 208\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 157\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://twitter.com/soraofficialapp/status/2036532795984715896","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47508246","date_published":"2026-03-24T20:01:05Z","author":{"name":"mikeocool","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=mikeocool"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47507150","title":"Wine 11 rewrites how Linux runs Windows games at kernel with massive speed gains","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.xda-developers.com/wine-11-rewrites-linux-runs-windows-games-speed-gains/\"\u003ehttps://www.xda-developers.com/wine-11-rewrites-linux-runs-windows-games-speed-gains/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47507150\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47507150\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 599\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 206\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.xda-developers.com/wine-11-rewrites-linux-runs-windows-games-speed-gains/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47507150","date_published":"2026-03-24T18:34:52Z","author":{"name":"felineflock","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=felineflock"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47506713","title":"Show HN: I took back Video.js after 16 years and we rewrote it to be 88% smaller","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you do when private equity buys your old company and fires the maintainers of the popular open source project you started over a decade ago? You reboot it, and bring along some new friends to do it.\u003cp\u003eVideo.js is used by billions of people every month, on sites like Amazon.com, Linkedin, and Dropbox, and yet it wasn’t in great shape. A skeleton crew of maintainers were doing their best with a dated architecture, but it needed more. So Sam from Plyr, Rahim from Vidstack, and Wes and Christain from Media Chrome jumped in to help me rebuild it better, faster, and smaller.\u003cp\u003eIt’s in beta now. Please give it a try and tell us what breaks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47506713\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47506713\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 131\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 10\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://videojs.org/blog/videojs-v10-beta-hello-world-again","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47506713","date_published":"2026-03-24T18:03:48Z","author":{"name":"Heff","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=Heff"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47506519","title":"FCC has banned the import of all new foreign-made routers here's what you can do","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://blog.adafruit.com/2026/03/24/fcc-just-banned-the-import-of-all-new-foreign-made-routers-heres-what-you-can-do-about-it/\"\u003ehttps://blog.adafruit.com/2026/03/24/fcc-just-banned-the-import-of-all-new-foreign-made-routers-heres-what-you-can-do-about-it/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47506519\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47506519\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u0